#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/library/ingest-l1-completeness-gate.bpmn:79
#. Diagram label
msgid "Adjudicate the flagged passage"
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/library/ingest-l1-completeness-gate.bpmn:96
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "All three converge on Task_Verdict, and that is deliberate rather than the codes being decoration: this lane adjudicates ONE passage while Lane_0 still owns the completeness verdict as a whole, so the outcome of a passage is a REASON recorded against that verdict, never a different next step. The same shape criterion-adjudication uses, where three outcomes converge on one write because what makes an outcome legitimate is that its reason was recorded. What differs is what gets written and what it obliges. `real` is drift to fix in the translation. `spurious` is a false positive, and recording it is what stops the same passage being re-flagged every run. `source-wrong` points at the SOURCE rather than the translation — the one answer that sends work out of this process entirely, because no amount of re-translating a wrong source produces a right target."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/library/ingest-l1-completeness-gate.bpmn:74
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Answered by the round-trip translation QA: did it flag semantic drift or a terminology miss? `drift` sends the passage to a person to adjudicate, since which reading is right is a human call; `clean` records the verdict directly."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/library/ingest-l1-completeness-gate.bpmn:68
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Back-translate each localized narrative into its source language and compare the meaning, to catch semantic drift and bad terminology that a forward-only check cannot see. Agentic. Two parties are kept apart under untainted-verification: a back-translator that sees ONLY the target-language text, and an adjudicator that sees the original and the back-translation and rules. The verdict is recorded per block, under criterion `translation-semantic-roundtrip` in the block's `<block>.<locale>.translation-qa.json` sidecar, by the `translation-roundtrip-record` Tool (translation-manager §5). A terminology miss is a different criterion, `translation-terms-preserved` (acronyms, numbers, URLs that must survive), so Gateway_Drift can tell the two apart. Never close this step by reversing the PO's msgid→msgstr map: that returns the source exactly and scores 1.0 always. An empty `translation-semantic-roundtrip` entry list means \"not yet run\", which is never a pass."
msgstr ""

